# Force LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference. The audit log is hash-chained: each record's
# digest is computed over its canonical bytes, so a checkout that rewrites
# LF to CRLF produces a chain that no longer matches its own hashes, and
# `driver-core verify` reports a chain as altered on Windows while
# verifying on Linux. Same evidence, two different verdicts, caused by the
# checkout rather than by anything anyone did.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The audit log and any other evidence file are bytes, not text.
*.jsonl -text
*.baseline.json -text

# Anything genuinely binary.
*.whl binary
*.png binary
